## Frequently Asked Questions

### 1. Is online therapy as effective as in-person therapy?

For some treatments and conditions, research suggests that online therapy can produce outcomes similar to in-person treatment. A 2024 systematic review of 54 randomized controlled trials found little to no difference between therapist-guided remote and in-person CBT across the primary outcomes studied. However, results should not be generalized to every treatment or individual.

### 2. Is face-to-face counseling better than virtual therapy?

Not necessarily. Face-to-face counseling may suit people who prefer a professional office environment, while online therapy may be more practical for those who value flexibility or have difficulty traveling. The best option depends on personal preferences, privacy, access, clinical needs, and therapist recommendations.

### 3. What are the disadvantages of online therapy?

Online therapy depends on suitable technology and a private environment. Internet interruptions, device problems, distractions, and difficulty finding a confidential space may affect the experience. Some services or clinical situations may also require in-person assessment or support.

### 4. Can I attend online therapy from anywhere in Texas?

That depends on the therapist's authorization, the practice's service area, and applicable licensing requirements. Riaz Counseling currently lists online therapy for people living throughout Texas. Confirm your eligibility and appointment options directly with the practice.

### 5. Do I need a private room for online counseling?

A private space is strongly recommended so you can speak openly without worrying about being overheard. If possible, use headphones, a password-protected device, and a private internet connection. If privacy at home is difficult, in-person counseling may be worth considering.

### 6. Can I change from online therapy to in-person counseling?

This may be possible if the practice offers both formats and the therapist has appropriate availability. Discuss the change with your therapist or the practice so they can confirm whether it is suitable for your needs.

### 7. Does Riaz Counseling offer both online and in-person therapy?

Yes. Riaz Counseling lists in-person services at its Houston Galleria, Sugar Land, and The Woodlands offices, as well as online therapy for people living throughout Texas. Contact the practice to confirm the current availability of the service and therapist you are considering.

## Conclusion: Choose the Therapy Format That Fits Your Needs

Comparing online and in-person therapy is not about deciding which format is universally superior. It is about understanding what each option offers and identifying the setting in which you can participate comfortably and consistently.

Online therapy may provide flexibility, reduce travel, and expand access to counseling. In-person counseling may offer a dedicated professional environment and the face-to-face interaction some people prefer.

Research supports the effectiveness of certain forms of remote therapy, including therapist-guided online CBT, but individual needs and clinical circumstances still matter.

If you are considering therapy, take time to think about your schedule, privacy, communication preferences, and the kind of support you need. You can also ask a qualified mental health professional to help you compare your options.

Riaz Counseling offers both in-person counseling in the Houston area and online therapy for people living in Texas. Exploring those options can be a practical first step toward finding mental health support that fits your life.

**You do not have to choose the format that works for everyone else. You can start by choosing the one that makes it possible for you to take the next step.**

### Mental Health Disclaimer

This article is intended for general educational purposes and does not replace professional mental health advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Online and in-person therapy may not be appropriate for every person or situation. A qualified mental health professional can help determine which services and format are suitable for your needs.

If you are experiencing an immediate mental health emergency or are at risk of harming yourself or someone else, seek urgent assistance through local emergency services or an appropriate crisis service.

